,"https://openalex.org/W2970971581","https://openalex.org/W3047146825","https://openalex.org/W3048402306","https://openalex.org/W3092948912","https://openalex.org/W3096718826","https://openalex.org/W3109476562","https://openalex.org/W3136327392","https://openalex.org/W3160458342","https://openalex.org/W3163847416","https://openalex.org/W3174752334","https://openalex.org/W3215589927","https://openalex.org/W4200150166","https://openalex.org/W4200382072","https://openalex.org/W4221151978","https://openalex.org/W4236965008","https://openalex.org/W4281651265","https://openalex.org/W4286615883","https://openalex.org/W4286750644","https://openalex.org/W4292387186","https://openalex.org/W4295308256","https://openalex.org/W4312325284","https://openalex.org/W4312706422","https://openalex.org/W4313165271","https://openalex.org/W4321488276","https://openalex.org/W4321512505","https://openalex.org/W4361194475","https://openalex.org/W4385318467","https://openalex.org/W4386066233","https://openalex.org/W4386071561","https://openalex.org/W4386075614","https://openalex.org/W4386075787","https://openalex.org/W4386076557","https://openalex.org/W4386076687","https://openalex.org/W4386273399","https://openalex.org/W4386453468","https://openalex.org/W4387725608","https://openalex.org/W4389540220","https://openalex.org/W4390723081","https://openalex.org/W4390871701","https://openalex.org/W4390872221","https://openalex.org/W4390872522","https://openalex.org/W4390874477","https://openalex.org/W4394593137","https://openalex.org/W4394596812","https://openalex.org/W4399574574","https://openalex.org/W4402660132","https://openalex.org/W4402713101","https://openalex.org/W6763422710","https://openalex.org/W6769157914","https://openalex.org/W6856152637","https://openalex.org/W6857808188","https://openalex.org/W7133190291","https://openalex.org/W7133245763"],"reviewed_benchmark_cells":[],"source":"arxiv","tags":["4DGS","Foundations"],"title":"4D Gaussian Splatting for Real-Time Dynamic Scene Rendering","tldr":"To achieve real-time dynamic scene rendering while also enjoying high training and storage efficiency we propose 4D Gaussian Splatting (4D-GS) as a holistic representation for dynamic scenes rather than...","updated_date":"2024-07-15","venue":"CVPR 2024","year":2023},"2310.08529":{"abstract":"In recent times, the generation of 3D assets from text prompts has shown impressive results. Both 2D and 3D diffusion models can help generate decent 3D objects based on prompts. 3D diffusion models have good 3D consistency, but their quality and generalization are limited as trainable 3D data is expensive and hard to obtain. 2D diffusion models enjoy strong abilities of generalization and fine generation, but 3D consistency is hard to guarantee. This paper attempts to bridge the power from the two types of diffusion models via the recent explicit and efficient 3D Gaussian splatting representation. A fast 3D object generation framework, named as GaussianDreamer, is proposed, where the 3D diffusion model provides priors for initialization and the 2D diffusion model enriches the geometry and appearance. Operations of noisy point growing and color perturbation are introduced to enhance the initialized Gaussians. Our GaussianDreamer can generate a high-quality 3D instance or 3D avatar within 15 minutes on one GPU, much faster than previous methods, while the generated instances can be directly rendered in real time. Demos and code are available at https://taoranyi.com/gaussiandreamer/.","arxiv_doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2310.08529","arxiv_id":"2310.08529","authors":["Taoran Yi","Jiemin Fang","Junjie Wang","Guanjun Wu","Lingxi Xie","Xiaopeng Zhang","Wenyu Liu","Qi Tian","Xinggang Wang"],"categories":["Human Avatars & VR","Generative Priors & 3D Reconstruction"],"citation_count":383,"citation_fetched_at":"2026-11-11T04:46:40.793522+00:00","citation_status":"ok","code_url":null,"comment":"CVPR 2024, Project page: https://taoranyi.com/gaussiandreamer/","date_placement":"observed"